hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"61","Allāhumma innī as'aluka al-jannata wa a'ūdhu bika min al-nār. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and seek Your protection from the Fire."
"62","Allāhumma bi-ʿilmika al-ghaybi wa-qudratika ʿalā al-khalqi aḥyinī mā ʿalimtu al-ḥayāta khayran lī, wa-tawaffanī idhā ʿalimtu al-wafāta khayran lī. Allāhumma innī asʾaluka khashyatak fī al-ghaybi wa-al-shahādah, wa-asʾaluka kalimata al-ḥaqq fī al-riḍā wa-al-ghaḍab, wa-asʾaluka al-qaṣda fī al-ghinā wa-al-faqr, asʾaluka naʿīman lā yanfad, wa-asʾaluka qurrata ʿaynin lā tanqaṭiʿ, wa-asʾaluka al-riḍā baʿda al-qaḍā, wa-asʾaluka barda al-ʿayshi baʿda al-mawt, wa-asʾaluka ladhdhata al-naẓar ilā wajhika wa-al-shawq ilā liqāʾik, fī ghayri ḍarrāʾ muḍirrā, wa-lā fitnatin muḍillā. Allāhumma zayyinnā bi-zīnat al-īmān, wa-jʿalunā hudātan muhtadīn.. O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as You know life is good for me, and take my soul when You know death is good for me. O Allah, I ask You for Your fear in private and in public, and I ask You for the word of truth in times of contentment and anger, and I ask You for moderation in wealth and poverty. I ask You for blessings that never end, and I ask You for the comfort of the eyes that never ceases, and I ask You for contentment after Your decree, and I ask You for the coolness of life after death, and I ask You for the joy of looking at Your Face and the longing to meet You, without any harmful hardship or misleading trial. O Allah, adorn us with the adornment of faith, and make us among the guided guides."
